sequenceDiagram
    title Mail Sort: durable classification and mailbox action queues

    actor Mailbox
    participant Collector as mail-collector
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Decision as mail-decision
    participant AI as AI model
    participant Router as mail-router
    participant Health as mail-health
    participant Alerts as mail-alerts
    participant PRTG
    participant Docker as Docker stdout
    participant Supervisor as mail-app supervisor

    Supervisor->>Collector: Start and monitor process
    Supervisor->>Decision: Start and monitor process
    Supervisor->>Router: Start and monitor process

    Mailbox->>Collector: Read new messages
    Collector->>DB: Save email_records and idempotent job
    Collector->>DB: Enqueue classify_email

    Decision->>DB: Claim classify_email (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)
    Decision->>DB: Read snapshot and active destinations
    Decision->>AI: Sender, subject, body, permitted destinations
    AI-->>Decision: destination_id and confidence
    Decision-->>Docker: JSON logs with job ID, message ID, subject, run ID
    Decision->>DB: Persist structured system log

    rect rgb(240, 246, 255)
        Note over Decision,DB: One database transaction
        Decision->>DB: Audit classification result
        Decision->>DB: Enqueue route_email
        Decision->>DB: Complete classify_email
    end

    Router->>DB: Claim route_email
    Router->>Mailbox: IMAP MOVE or EWS MoveItem
    Router-->>Docker: JSON logs with job ID, message ID, subject
    Router->>DB: Persist structured system log
    alt Provider confirms move
        Router->>DB: Complete route_email
    else Provider unavailable or fails
        Router->>DB: Retry route_email with delay
        opt Retry budget exhausted
            Router->>DB: Set failed and enqueue critical alert atomically
        end
    end

    PRTG->>Health: GET /health/ready
    Health->>Supervisor: GET /health/services
    Health->>DB: SELECT 1
    Health->>AI: Check provider API and configured model
    Health-->>PRTG: 200 ready or 503 degraded
    Alerts->>DB: Claim pending alert with SKIP LOCKED
    Alerts->>PRTG: Push alert data to HTTP Push Data Advanced sensor
    Alerts->>DB: Mark delivered or retry later
